  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of National Tuberculosis Program - Syrian Arab Republic (01-Jun-2013-31-Dec-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As in many other countries in the region, TB continues to be a major communicable disease in the Syrian Arab Republic. This grant will be used to address the low case detection rate and to contribute to reducing the gaps identified in the Syrian Arab Republic&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s ten-year strategic plan by improving access to TB care, particularly for poor and vulnerable populations; addressing multidrug-resistant TB (MDR-TB); engaging all care providers; strengthening the health system; and encouraging advocacy, communication and social mobilization. The program targets poor urban and rural areas of the five northeastern governorates; poverty pockets in the rural areas of the middle and coastal governorates; vulnerable groups at high risk of developing TB, in particular TB contacts and prisoners; and patients with MDR-TB.</narrative>
  </description>
